.TXT 38 4 120 0
Cg a65.875000,66.250000,278
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain From the explicit FR form above,
 at {\f1 w} = - {\f1 p}, the overall phase
 should be 0, which it is: thus the {\f1 
p}/2 phase shift which produces the i = 
sqrt(-1) is indeed observed. Also, as sin({\f1 
w}) changes sign at {\f1 w} = 0, there is
 a phase shift of {\f1 p} there.}
}
.TXT 12 0 65 0
Cg a65.625000,65.875000,157
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
